# Drafted by Gemini (R25 endings), edited.

~ start
Narrator: In the deep of the Wytchwood, the Crooked Tree burns down to white ash, and the dark queen is bound tight within the pale prison of the moon.
Narrator: Four bright embers rose from the goat skull to seal that lock, leaving only quiet moss and cold stone behind.
Narrator: Down by the edge of the moor, a ghost-blue headlamp cuts through the rolling fog as the Ghostlight Express pulls in along the iron rails.
Narrator: Steam hisses against the damp heather while four brass tickets sit waiting on the conductor's velvet bench, paid in full and unclaimed.
Narrator: The Vagrant steps down to the empty timber platform, takes off his battered cap, and holds it against his chest in the hush.
the_vagrant [sad]: Four good fares paid their way at the root, and left me with an empty car to haul.
Narrator: He sets his cap back on his head, shifts the sprig of wheat between his teeth, and climbs aboard the silent carriage.
Narrator: The whistle blows once, low and mournful across the valley, and the train rolls out into the fog with every velvet seat bare.
-> END
